                            <comment id="16096184" author="kukushal" created="Fri, 21 Jul 2017 12:28:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This likely a duplicate for &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5505&quot; title=&quot;@AffinityKeyMapped annotation is ignored if class names are configured on BinaryConfiguration&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-5505&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-5505&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; that I am working on now. Assigned this one to myself to test the fix.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16114478" author="kukushal" created="Fri, 4 Aug 2017 15:03:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I discussed this with &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=vozerov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;vozerov&quot;&gt;vozerov&lt;/a&gt; and confirmed we do not want to fix this since any fix would violate Ignite design ideology. &lt;br/&gt;
To work around the problem in addition to specifying affinity key field using @AffinityKeyMapped annotation also specify it in the cache key configuration like this:&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;property name=&quot;cacheConfiguration&quot;&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;list&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;bean class=&quot;org.apache.ignite.configuration.CacheConfiguration&quot;&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
...&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;property name=&quot;keyConfiguration&quot;&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;bean class=&quot;org.apache.ignite.cache.CacheKeyConfiguration&quot;&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;property name=&quot;typeName&quot; value=&quot;TYPE_NAME&quot;/&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;property name=&quot;affinityKeyFieldName&quot; value=&quot;AFFINITY_KEY_FIELD_NAME&quot;/&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;/bean&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;/property&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;/bean&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;/list&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&amp;lt;/property&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Resolving this issue with a fix.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
